5.8 Interview questions
Q1. What are embeddings in Generative AI?

Embeddings are numerical representations of text, images or other data in a vector space. They help systems identify semantic relationships and retrieve relevant information.

Q2. Why do we generate embeddings in RAG?

We generate embeddings to convert document chunks and user queries into vectors. This allows us to retrieve semantically relevant information using vector similarity search.

Q3. What is embedding dimension?

Embedding dimension is the number of numerical values in a vector. Our all-MiniLM-L6-v2 model generates 384-dimensional vectors.

Q4. Why should we use the same embedding model for documents and queries?

The document and query vectors must be compatible in the same vector space. Using the same model is the simplest way to ensure this compatibility.

Q5. What is the difference between an embedding model and an LLM?

An embedding model converts text into numerical vectors. An LLM generates or understands responses based on input text and its learned parameters. They perform different roles in a RAG system.
